115
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:23,000
The Historical Society would like to work with the school district as consultants to help you move forward

116
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:27,000
with helping embracing the history of the academy.

117
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:34,000
The academy goes... the 1803 building, as you all know, but you know the academy was first built in the 1780s.

118
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
That burned down in fire.

119
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Some of the rich history that academy has.

120
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:45,000
President John Adams sent six of his grandchildren to the academy.

121
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:52,000
And they probably lived at the Kimball House, which is the old Peabody home from Reverend Peabody.

122
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:57,000
John Adams visited Atkinson and stayed at the Peabody home.

123
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:01,000
So we're asking you to work with us.

124
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Let us work with you and help you embellish the history of the academy.

125
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:13,000
One of our members, Pam Alexander, is working on the history of the academy that she's on staff with you,

126
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:18,000
that she wants to share with the students of the academy and also with the residents.

127
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:27,000
So there's so much that building could bring to light and to embrace its history to share with the students.

128
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:36,000
One, as if you want to apply for grants, as the school embraces its history and shares it with the students, helps the grants.

129
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:41,000
They want to know that the school is being preserved.

130
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:45,000
So I'm just here to say we are not volunteering to do it.

131
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
But as you know, we're in the middle of the schoolhouse.

132
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:52,000
I don't know if you're aware of the center schoolhouse restoration in Atkinson.

133
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:57,000
We're restoring Atkinson's last one remaining schoolroom, which is right across the street from the academy.

134
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:01,000
And we're already talking to teachers of what we're going to do in the near future.

135
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:07,000
So I'm here to offer that service to help you move forward with preserving the history.

