214
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:27,000
First, the annual report first on the agenda here.

215
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
So just a couple of quick highlights.

216
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Great, great, great year last year.

217
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:40,000
During the 25-26 school year, the athletic department put on approximately 807 events between middle school and high school for the year.

218
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,000
That's not including practices.

219
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,000
That's just all games, tournaments, playoffs, et cetera.

220
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:52,000
Throughout the year, we had approximately 739 middle school and high school kids participating in athletics.

221
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:56,000
And out of those student athletes, 41% played multiple sports.

222
00:09:56,000 --> 00:10:03,000
We had 433 kids in one sport, 188 playing two and 118 playing three.

223
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,000
So we're really happy about that.

224
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Middle school athletic update.

225
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:12,000
And I want to thank Mr. Zach Champion, the middle school coordinator last year for this.

226
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:19,000
The Timberlake Middle School Athletic Program is a member of the Tri-County League and competes against schools from around the state in New Hampshire.

227
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:28,000
The purpose of the Tri-County League is to organize, coordinate, and stimulate interest in athletic activities while developing young athletes at the middle school level.

228
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:34,000
The Tigers enjoyed an outstanding athletic year with more than 312 student athletes participating during the year.

229
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:41,000
And our student athletes and coaches represented Timberlake with pride, achieving success across multiple sports.

230
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:47,000
During the winter season, the girls wrestling team made school history by finishing second in the state championship.

231
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,000
It was the highest finish in their program's history.

232
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:57,000
The boys basketball team had an exciting run and made it to the finals for that season.

233
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:02,000
And in the spring, the continued momentum with several impressive accomplishments.

234
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:05,000
The girls' A softball team advanced to the finals.

235
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:16,000
And also, this is something that we're really proud of, the girls' track and field team put together a dominant season, winning every meet that they competed in before capturing the Tri-County Championships.

236
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,000
But here's the wonderful thing.

237
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:29,000
The championships were especially meaningful as it was held at Timberlake's new track and allowed us to host the Tri-County Championships for the first time in more than a decade.

238
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:36,000
At the high school level, we compete in the New Hampshire Interscholastic Athletic Association.

239
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,000
You know that as the NHIA.

240
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:45,000
We are a recognized Division I athletic program, and we offer over 30 sports programs for our kids.

241
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Another thing that we're very proud of is many of our student athletes are also involved in a variety of activities, including band, music, and student government.

242
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:56,000
The athletic program enjoyed tremendous success throughout the year.

243
00:11:56,000 --> 00:12:05,000
The wrestling team captured the Division I state championship, and our winter cheer team finished as runner-ups at the state meet.

244
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Spring was incredible.

245
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:11,000
All of our sports teams qualified for the state tournament.

246
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:16,000
We had girls lacrosse, baseball, and softball all making it to the state semifinals.

247
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
It was an exciting spring.

248
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Aside from team honors, we had some really impressive individual achievements.

249
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:31,000
We had rising senior Danielle Bates, who was the state champ in the high jump and the triple jump.

250
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:40,000
And recent graduate Charlotte Baldwin was not just a state champ, but she broke four school records in the process during track.

251
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Also in lacrosse, we had Lila Fitzgerald and Riley Donahue reach milestones by scoring their 100th career goal.

252
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:54,000
This I am especially proud of because I think we should be honoring our coaches.

253
00:12:54,000 --> 00:13:03,000
Football coach Kevin Fitzgerald has been awarded the 2025 NFHS Football Coaches Award for the state of New Hampshire.

254
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:09,000
This award recognizes outstanding football coaches through its Coaching Association Awards,

255
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:14,000
