00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:35,000
But I do see a lot of value in this proposed schedule for all the reasons that you just shared, Mitch.

785
00:37:35,000 --> 00:37:43,000
But also I'm thinking in terms of like student experience, my own kiddos experience, seventh grade math was a deep, deep challenge.

786
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:50,000
And having essentially nine classes was really a struggle.

787
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:58,000
And so when I communicated with Mr. McCarthy as the assistant principal of the seventh grade, we chatted about some different ideas and he really did need more support and win.

788
00:37:58,000 --> 00:38:00,000
But that meant that he and that was wonderful.

789
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:01,000
And he needed it at that time.

790
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:03,000
And you guys were flexible about the schedule.

791
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:05,000
But then he had to give up something.

792
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:10,000
And that was kind of, you know, one of those conversations you have to have with your kid.

793
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:20,000
And I know Bill worked with him, too, to kind of say, like, what's the priority right now, you know, and this schedule would allow for that opportunity to happen every day.

794
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:38,000
And I think as a board member outside of the parent, I really think the idea of kids having win what I need every day to provide really structured and targeted supports is a complement to a lot of the work that you guys have already initiated.

795
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:57,000
The middle school about the dreaded standardized testing and making those connections earlier on in the year before you get to the testing and assessment period will then hopefully help with some competency increases in our testing overall.

796
00:38:57,000 --> 00:39:00,000
So I think this is great.

797
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:09,000
And I think it's a really creative solution to not necessarily a problem, like you said, because it was working.

798
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:18,000
But I love the continuous evaluation and hearing the voices of the teachers, too, to be able to speak to this.

799
00:39:18,000 --> 00:39:25,000
So thank you for bringing this to us because I think it's going to be beneficial to the students at the middle school.

